    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d791">

                <pb facs="0725" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/2575</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 17, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5846. Your 7714, 16th. Please acknowledge to Foreign Office and state that no
                    scheme, if any, will be presented which would interfere with the military
                    necessities of the Allies. Matter is held in abeyance pending clearing up of
                    political situation as regards Russia’s attitude.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
